I walk down to the little shop on the corner.
The baskets stand by the door.
I take a basket and walk in.
First I find a lightbulb.
There are lightbulbs lying on the bottom shelf.
I take one and put it in the basket.
I also find coffee and a little food for dinner.
But there is no milk.
"Excuse me, where is the milk?" I ask a man.
"It is in the fridge over there," says the man.
"Thank you very much," I say.
I walk over to the fridge.
The milk is standing in the fridge.
Now my basket is full.
I pay at the till.
Then I walk home to my new flat.
